{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1896, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nOn a certain planet, there are N aliens, all of whom are minors.\nThe i-th alien currently has A_i stones, and will become an adult exactly i years later.\nWhen someone becomes an adult on this planet, every adult who has at least one stone gives exactly one stone as a congratulatory gift to the alien who has just become an adult.\nFind how many stones each alien will have after N years.\nAssume that no new aliens will be born in the future.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN\r\nA_1 A_2 \\ldots A_N\n\nOutput\n\nLet B_i be the number of stones owned by the i-th alien after N years. Print B_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_N in this order, separated by spaces.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 1 \\leq N \\leq 5 \\times 10^5\n- 0 \\leq A_i \\leq 5 \\times 10^5\n- All input values are integers.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n4\r\n5 0 9 3\n\nSample Output 1\n\n2 0 10 5\r\n\nLet C_i be the number of stones that the i-th alien has at a given time.\nInitially, (C_1, C_2, C_3, C_4) = (5, 0, 9, 3).\nAfter 1 year, (C_1, C_2, C_3, C_4) = (5, 0, 9, 3).\nAfter 2 years, (C_1, C_2, C_3, C_4) = (4, 1, 9, 3).\nAfter 3 years, (C_1, C_2, C_3, C_4) = (3, 0, 11, 3).\nAfter 4 years, (C_1, C_2, C_3, C_4) = (2, 0, 10, 5).\n\nSample Input 2\n\n5\r\n4 6 7 2 5\n\nSample Output 2\n\n0 4 7 4 9\n\nSample Input 3\n\n10\r\n2 9 1 2 0 4 6 7 1 5\n\nSample Output 3\n\n0 2 0 0 0 4 7 10 4 10\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1941, "char_start": 1908, "quote": "Input:\n4\n5 0 9 3\nOutput:\n2 0 10 5", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1989, "char_start": 1953, "quote": "Input:\n5\n4 6 7 2 5\nOutput:\n0 4 7 4 9", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R5", "source": {"char_end": 2060, "char_start": 2001, "quote": "Input:\n10\n2 9 1 2 0 4 6 7 1 5\nOutput:\n0 2 0 0 0 4 7 10 4 10", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 3: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "213a37cd777f6f5808f381a2b6eb10949cb5d29f81ac45e71c5f23a4858b0db2", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "988eb0ce0c0c5658180b94bf97c6c9f7279723dfa820ba65bfc5c6506602bc9b", "seq": 2}
